## Start with one responsibility

A small application is easier to understand when each part has a clear job. Routing accepts a request. Validation checks the input. Application logic decides what should happen. Storage keeps the result.

These boundaries do not require separate services. A handful of functions and modules can be enough.

## Make failure understandable

Give errors names that explain what went wrong. Distinguish an invalid request from a missing record and from an unavailable dependency. The next person reading a log should have a useful starting point.

## Grow when there is a reason

Keep the design close to the problem you actually have. Add complexity when it removes a concrete limitation, and write down the trade-off.

